6. Assembler

This section presents a basic assembler that translates assembly instructions into 16-bit machine code executable by the computer. 
It recognises A- and C-instructions, parses their components, and converts operation, destination, and jump mnemonics into hexadecimal fields.
This version supports only numerical addresses; symbolic labels, variables, and symbol-table processing are not implemented. 

Java source code of and assembler is located in the Java_assembler file. 
Source code - Assembler.java 

Main method is reading command line arguments for the "intputFile" that contains mnemonics. 

How to start the program: 
java Assembler Program.asm


Files for testing the system are located in Computer_Validation_Tests file.
One can run those programs in Assembler and get corresponding hex file to insert into the ROM, but dont forget to put values in RAM if you have input values that work with memory.
